(AetherCorp Engineering Standards) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Document ID: ENG-STD-2026) Tj
T*
(Audience: Software engineering, SRE, data) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Source control) Tj
T*
(The default branch is main. Feature work happens on branches named feat/<ticket>-<slug>.) Tj
T*
(Pull requests require one approving review and a green CI pipeline. Direct pushes to main) Tj
T*
(are blocked.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Python) Tj
T*
(Services use Python 3.13, uv for lockfiles, and Ruff for linting. Public functions must) Tj
T*
(have type hints. FastAPI is the standard HTTP framework.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Observability) Tj
T*
(Every inference call must emit an OpenTelemetry span. Traces are exported to Arize Phoenix.) Tj
T*
(Service logs use structured JSON. RED metrics \(rate, errors, duration\) are required for) Tj
T*
(user-facing APIs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Incident response) Tj
T*
(Sev-1: customer-facing outage or data loss. Page the on-call engineer and open an incident) Tj
T*
(channel named inc-YYYYMMDD-shortname. A written postmortem is due within 3 business days.) Tj
T*
(Sev-2: degraded performance. Respond within 30 minutes during business hours.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Secrets) Tj
T*
(Secrets live in the platform vault. They must never be committed to git. Rotate leaked) Tj
T*
(credentials within 1 hour.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Retrieval systems) Tj
T*
(Production RAG services store embeddings in PostgreSQL with pgvector. Embedding dimension) Tj
T*
(must match the configured model. Hybrid search \(vector + keyword\) is required for policy) Tj
T*
(corpora.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. On-call) Tj
T*
(Primary on-call rotates weekly. Handoff is Friday 16:00 UTC. The on-call engineer must have) Tj
T*
(laptop access and the production runbook at https://runbooks.aethercorp.example.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
